 "CT-mystic":[
  ["Abbott's Lobster in the Rough","Hot lobster roll","Outdoor picnic tables on Noank harbour, BYO wine, closed in winter."],
  ["Anthony J's","","A classic Italian bistro featuring imported pasta and some American fare. Be sure to explore the wine selection."],
  ["Bravo, Bravo & Bar","","Fine Italian dining for $20-25."],
  ["Go Fish","","Olde Mistick Village, 23 Coogan Boulevard. M-Th 11:30AM-9:30PM, F Sa 11:30AM-10PM, Su noon-9:30PM. Enjoy the best seafood in Mystic anyway you like it; cooked or raw for an experience at the sushi bar."],
  ["Kitchen Little","","(Route 27). A small shack-like building on your way into Mystic. This has the best breakfast around. The service is friendly and they are quick to refill your java. The sausage and home fries are great and so is the charm. Dining inside is packed tight with tables, but your reward will be worth the squeeze. They offer loads of vegetarian options but very little (other than a veggie wrap around lunch) for vegans. Under $10 for a hearty breakfast."],
  ["Mystic Pizza","","No Julia Roberts doesn't work there; you can check out the sweet 1988 romantic comedy if you want to see her dish up something nice. Otherwise this is your go-to spot for tourist grub. Enjoy at under $20 for entree or pizza."],
  ["Mezza Mediterranean Cuisine","","Rt. 1. An interesting alternative for a dining experience in Mystic, The Pita Spot boasts a Mediterranean menu unlike any other in the area. Enjoy an American breakfast, or a Mediterranean lunch and dinner outside during the summer, or inside during the winter. A tourist hot-spot, The Pita Spot is small and cozy with service that will tend to your every need."],
  ["S&P Oyster Co","","Close to many of Mystic's attractions, this restaurant draws crowds for its fantastic seafood. In the summertime, diners can sit on the outdoor patio and enjoy the seaport. $20-30."],
  ["Steak Loft","","Fine dining and an olde tyme atmosphere. Voted Connecticut magazine \"Best Steak\", and rightfully so! Expect to pay about $25 for their top-rated steaks."],
  ["The Captain Daniel Packer Inne, Restaurant and Pub","","Built over 250 years ago, this restaurant is two stories. The lower floor is a small pub, the upper story is a restaurant. They have two different menus, both excellent. Particularly good, and reasonably priced, are the fish and chips and burgers in the pub. Arrive early to get a table in the pub section. If none are available, the more expensive restaurant section is also worth the visit."],
  ["Angies Pizza","","Enjoy the expansive Greek menu of this local hotspot. This quiet yet bustling restaurant has extremely reliable service and quality. A very relaxed dining experience."],
  ["Mystic Drawbridge Ice Cream","","Next to the bridge that is part of its namesake, this small ice cream parlor serves a varied menu of frozen treats with something for everyone. Open during Summer and Winter, their menu includes a wide spectrum of choices from salads and sandwiches to ice cream, malts, and pastries. Their ice cream offerings include over 25 varieties, made with a number of local ingredients."]],

 "CT-new-haven":[
  ["Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana","White clam pie","Coal-fired since 1925, and the clam pie is not optional."],
  ["Louis' Lunch","Hamburger sandwich","Claims the first hamburger, 1900, broiled vertically. No ketchup, and they mean it."],
  ["Libbys Italian Cookies and Pastries","","Amazing cookies, cannoli, Italian pastries, Italian ice, and coffee."],
  ["Aladdin Crown Pizza","","Don't be fooled by the name; the best cuisine this place offers is not pizza; it's Middle Eastern. Be sure to try their falafel plate and baclava dessert. Authentic food with excellent service."],
  ["Claire's Corner Copia","","Vegan and vegetarian options, regularly-changing specials. Known for their Lithuanian coffee cake. Great bakery with gluten-free options. Kosher."],
  ["Pacifico","","Latin American seafood dishes with an upscale New York sensibility served at this LGBT-friendly restaurant."],
  ["Union League Café","","Upscale French cuisine. Make reservations."],
  ["York St. Noodle House","","If you're looking for an inexpensive, casual meal, York St. Noodle House is the place to go. Service is always friendly, and the menu always has irresistible options. Be sure to try their delicious boba fruit slushy. Try also coconut curry noodle soup and spicy wok basil noodle."],
  ["Yorkside Pizza and Restaurant","","Family-owned diner with large menu and very reasonable prices. Dough and sauces are made fresh daily on the premises."],
  ["Zinc","","Modern American. Chef's table options focus on local food items. Make reservations."],
  ["Encore by Goodfellas","","This is the perfect place not only for the connoisseur of Italian cuisine but for also a lover of movies. You can enjoy some of the finest Italian food New Haven has to offer while viewing movie classics on their ten flatscreen televisions"],
  ["Sally's Apizza","",""]],

